// Hand-authored traffic policy overrides for Cromatolis's maritime routes.
//
// This file is NOT generated by `xindeler-open-world` and has no mask
// behind it -- unlike everything in `assets/world/map/`, which is export
// output. It deliberately lives in a sibling directory of its own,
// `assets/world/maritime/`, so it is never mistaken for a regenerable
// export (the same posture `assets/world/wildlife/` already uses for
// `cromatolis_v0_density_boost.ron`).
//
// Every field is optional: an absent field means "use the engine's
// computed default" -- `LongHaul` if a route's `length_m` is at least
// 8,000m, else `Coastal`; a random 4-8 ship roll per route, deterministic
// from the route id and the world seed; every route carries
// `[Cargo, Passengers]`. This file may ship empty, and does today: it is a
// correction surface for tuning traffic by hand, not something that needs
// real overrides to be authored yet.
(
    schema: "xindeler.cromatolis_maritime_traffic.v1",
    routes: [],
    settlements: [],
    world_ship_budget: None,
)
